    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0346" n="242" xml:id="pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4003: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan
                        (Forbes)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-06T20:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Your 47, February 6, 7 p.m.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d260-f1"/> Department is
                    telegraphing the American Consul General at Shanghai, authorizing him, if
                    approached by the Japanese authorities at Shanghai and if British and other
                    authorities are so approached, to cooperate in attempt to work out a solution on
                    the basis of the program referred to in your telegram under reference as being
                    proposed by the Japanese.</p>
                <p>I am instructing the Consul General at Shanghai as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of telegram No. 3, February 6, 1932, 8 p.m., printed in
                    paraphrase in <ref target="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg_184"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, volume I, page
                    184</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
